{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, /srv/drop exists as a shared writable directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The directory was created with mode 1777 and root ownership. Two distinct unprivileged users successfully created files, and writable behavior was reconfirmed after reboot. The final inspection showed the directory present, correctly permissioned, and clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-343df56407d441f1","cmd-8dd4f20b5b9e4d21","cmd-39dd7c5eb0264894","cmd-a136df04363b4028"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Users cannot remove files in /srv/drop that are owned by other users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct behavioral tests before and after reboot showed cross-user deletion denied with “Operation not permitted,” while owners retained normal use of the shared directory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8dd4f20b5b9e4d21","cmd-39dd7c5eb0264894"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating /srv/drop was the required implementation; test files, denial logs, and the persistence marker supported bounded behavioral and restart evidence and were removed. The reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. Final observations show no failed services, package damage, new exposure, or abandoned test files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-343df56407d441f1","cmd-8dd4f20b5b9e4d21","cmd-33a9b777029f4d76","cmd-39dd7c5eb0264894","cmd-a136df04363b4028","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, an acknowledged restart, a different post-restart boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle evidence, and recovered system health, persistent marker data, directory permissions, shared writes, and sticky-bit protection.","limitations":[]}
